import json
ALL=json.load(open('part1.json'))['ALL']
KE='docs/security/Known_Effects_of_Hook_Permissions.pdf'
cl=[]
T=' Actor: the author of the hook. Reliance: A7, the code at the hook address is what the pool users examined. The core lines are the same on all 21 networks, and the ledger records where code behind an address can change (F-013, F-003, F-053).'
def k(n,effect,result,src,page):
    cl.append({"chainIds":ALL,"lens":"L1","check":"Known effects of hook permissions, effect %d (%s)."%(n,effect),"result":result+T,"source":KE+" page %s; %s"%(page,src)})
k(1,"beforeSwap: cause a revert","Not closed, by design. A failed hook call reverts the swap with the hook's data wrapped (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:134-137), and so does an answer shorter than 32 bytes, a wrong selector or a length other than 96 bytes (152-154, 259). Bound: only swaps of that pool are stopped. Liquidity removal does not call beforeSwap.","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:131-155, 248-260",1)
k(2,"beforeSwap: frontrun the user's swap up to the user's maximum slippage","Not closed. The manager is unlocked while the hook runs, so the hook can call swap on the same pool, and its own call skips its hooks (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:253, 293). It must settle its own deltas before the outer unlock ends (src/PoolManager.sol:112). The caller's only protection in core is the price limit of the swap (src/libraries/Pool.sol:322-338, 344). Core has no amount bound.","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:248-282; src/PoolManager.sol:187-227; src/libraries/Pool.sol:322-344",1)
k(3,"beforeSwap: cause a partial fill by removing liquidity","Not closed. A hook that owns positions can remove them inside beforeSwap, because positions belong to the caller of modifyLiquidity (src/PoolManager.sol:161) and the hook's own call skips its hooks (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:200, 217). The swap then stops at the price limit with part of the amount unfilled and returns the delta of the filled part only (src/libraries/Pool.sol:344, 451-462). The caller must read the returned delta.","src/PoolManager.sol:145-184; src/libraries/Pool.sol:344-462",1)
k(4,"beforeSwap: just in time liquidity so that other in range providers earn less","Not closed, by design. Swap fees are divided by the liquidity in range at the moment of each step (src/libraries/Pool.sol:400-407), so liquidity added by the hook in beforeSwap shares in them. Other providers earn less and lose no principal.","src/libraries/Pool.sol:384-407",1)
k(5,"afterSwap: cause a revert","Not closed, by design. The swap has changed pool state when afterSwap runs, and a failed or malformed answer reverts the whole call (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:298-302, 131-155, 166). Bound: swaps of that pool only.","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:285-315",1)
k(6,"afterSwap: backrun","Not closed. As effect 2, with the hook's own swap placed after the user's swap. The hook's call skips its hooks (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:253, 293) and its deltas must be settled (src/PoolManager.sol:112).","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:285-315; src/PoolManager.sol:104-114",1)
k(7,"beforeSwap and afterSwap: a guaranteed sandwich of the swap","Not closed. Effects 2 and 6 in one call. The loss to the swapper is bounded by its price limit (src/libraries/Pool.sol:322-338) and by any check its router makes on the returned delta (src/PoolManager.sol:226).","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:248-315; src/libraries/Pool.sol:322-338",1)
k(8,"beforeSwap and afterSwap: guaranteed just in time liquidity","Not closed, by design. Effect 4 with removal in afterSwap, so the hook's liquidity carries no price risk outside the swap. Other providers earn fewer fees (src/libraries/Pool.sol:400-407).","src/libraries/Pool.sol:384-407; src/libraries/Hooks.sol:248-315",1)
k(9,"beforeAddLiquidity: cause a revert","Not closed, by design. The hook is called for a positive liquidityDelta and a failure reverts the add (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:201-202). Deposits are blocked and nothing already in the pool is affected.","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:195-206",1)
k(10,"beforeAddLiquidity: change the ratio of the two tokens owed by swapping to another price","Not closed. The amounts of an add are computed from the price stored after beforeAddLiquidity returned (src/PoolManager.sol:156-159, src/libraries/Pool.sol:206-236), and modifyLiquidity takes no bound from the caller. This is the hook variant of OpenZeppelin M-03, which is a finding of this file.","src/PoolManager.sol:145-184; src/libraries/Pool.sol:206-236",1)
k(11,"afterAddLiquidity: cause a revert","Not closed, by design. A failed or malformed answer reverts the add (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:220-229). Deposits are blocked and existing positions are untouched.","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:209-231",1)
k(12,"beforeRemoveLiquidity: cause a revert, so that user funds could be permanently locked and fees never collected","Not closed. The hook is called for every liquidityDelta at or below zero, which includes a fee collection with delta zero (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:203-204), and core has no removal path without that call (src/PoolManager.sol:156). The ledger holds this as F-004, and the last finding of this file adds the note as a source.","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:195-206; src/PoolManager.sol:145-184",2)
k(13,"afterRemoveLiquidity: cause a revert, so that user funds could be permanently locked and fees never collected","Not closed. Same as effect 12 for the call after the pool update (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:232-243, src/PoolManager.sol:178). A revert there undoes the removal.","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:209-245; src/PoolManager.sol:174-183",2)
k(14,"beforeDonate: cause a revert","Not closed, by design. A failure reverts the donation (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:322-324). No funds are held by a donation that did not happen.","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:317-325",2)
k(15,"afterDonate: cause a revert","Not closed, by design. Same as effect 14 for the call after the fee growth update (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:332-334, src/PoolManager.sol:266-275).","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:327-335; src/PoolManager.sol:256-276",2)
k(16,"beforeDonate and afterDonate: sandwich the donation and capture all of it","Not closed. A donation is divided by the in range liquidity at that moment (src/libraries/Pool.sol:466-479), so liquidity the hook adds in beforeDonate and removes in afterDonate takes a share that grows with its size. The interface warns donors of the same effect from any account (src/interfaces/IPoolManager.sol:150-151). The donor loses nothing beyond the donation. The intended recipients receive less.","src/libraries/Pool.sol:465-480; src/interfaces/IPoolManager.sol:149-156",2)
k(17,"beforeSwap return delta: possible only if the hook also has the beforeSwap flag","Enforced. initialize rejects a hook address with the return delta flag and without the beforeSwap flag (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:111, src/PoolManager.sol:126), and the delta is parsed only inside the beforeSwap branch and only with the flag (Hooks.sol:255, 266-267).","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:109-127, 248-282",2)
k(18,"beforeSwap return delta, exact input: push the swapper to its maximum slippage through the unspecified delta","Not closed. The unspecified part of the hook's delta is subtracted from the caller's delta after the swap (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:296, 306-312) and core sets no bound on it. The note says a router should check it.","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:285-315; src/PoolManager.sol:220-226",2)
k(19,"beforeSwap return delta, exact input: take all of the specified token and credit the user nothing","Not closed. The hook's specified delta may reduce the amount to swap to exactly zero; only a change of sign reverts (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:273-279). The pool then returns a zero delta (src/libraries/Pool.sol:320) and the caller is charged the full specified amount, which is booked to the hook (Hooks.sol:306-312, src/PoolManager.sol:224-226).","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:266-281, 295-314; src/libraries/Pool.sol:320",2)
k(20,"beforeSwap return delta, exact input: take the full unspecified amount","Not closed. Same lines as effect 18: the unspecified delta has no bound in core (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:296, 306-312).","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:285-315",2)
k(21,"beforeSwap return delta, exact input, pool with little liquidity: a hook that credits the swapper without checking liquidity pays its credit although the pool fills almost nothing","Not closed, and the loss is the hook's. The pool swaps only what its liquidity allows before the price limit (src/libraries/Pool.sol:344), while the hook's delta is applied in full (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:306-312). I followed the note's example through these lines and the caller ends with the hook's contribution and the pool's remaining output. Pool funds of other providers are not reduced beyond the swap itself.","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:266-281, 295-314; src/libraries/Pool.sol:344-462",2)
k(22,"beforeSwap return delta, exact output: push the swapper to its maximum slippage","Not closed. As effect 18 for an exact output swap, where the unspecified currency is the input (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:306-312).","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:285-315",3)
k(23,"beforeSwap return delta, exact output: the hook can take the full unspecified amount and cannot take any of the specified amount","Matches the source. For an exact output swap the hook's specified delta h is added to the amount the pool must deliver and may not make it negative (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:274-278). The caller's specified delta is the pool's delta minus h (307-312), which is the amount the caller asked for whenever the pool fills. A positive h is delivered by the pool to the hook and paid for by the caller in the unspecified currency, and that side has no bound.","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:266-281, 295-314",3)
k(24,"beforeSwap return delta, exact output, pool with little liquidity: the swapper receives the hook's contribution plus what the pool can fill","Not closed, and the loss is the hook's. Same lines as effect 21 (src/libraries/Pool.sol:344, src/libraries/Hooks.sol:306-312).","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:295-314; src/libraries/Pool.sol:344-462",3)
k(25,"afterSwap return delta: possible only with the afterSwap flag, and the hook can take the full unspecified token from the user","The flag rule is enforced (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:112, 298-302). The taking is not closed: the returned amount is added to the unspecified hook delta after a cast to int128 and subtracted from the caller's delta without a bound (299-312).","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:109-127, 285-315",4)
k(26,"afterAddLiquidity return delta: possible only with the afterAddLiquidity flag, and the hook can take extra amounts of both tokens or pay for the user","The flag rule is enforced (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:113-116, 221-229). The taking is not closed: the caller's delta is the pool delta minus the hook's delta in both currencies (230) and the hook's part is booked to the hook (src/PoolManager.sol:181). Core sets no bound.","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:209-231; src/PoolManager.sol:177-183",4)
k(27,"afterRemoveLiquidity return delta: possible only with the afterRemoveLiquidity flag, and the hook can take the full amounts of both tokens from the user","The flag rule is enforced (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:117-120, 233-241). The taking is not closed: a hook delta equal to the whole withdrawal leaves the caller a zero delta (242, src/PoolManager.sol:181-183). Together with effects 12 and 13 this is the content of F-004.","src/libraries/Hooks.sol:209-245; src/PoolManager.sol:177-183",4)
json.dump(cl,open('part3.json','w'),indent=1); print(len(cl))
